.TH VOCABULARY 1
.SH NAME
vocabulary \- vocabulary quiz
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B temple/vocabulary
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Vocabulary
is the TempleOS vocabulary quiz.
It runs under
.IR wm (1).
.PP
A word is shown in blinking red, followed by four numbered
definitions from the dictionary; choose the definition that matches
the word.
After each answer the full dictionary entry of the quizzed word pops
up so you learn it; dismiss the popup and the next round is already
waiting.
A high tone marks a correct answer, a low tone a wrong one.
.PP
The controls are:
.TF space
.TP
.B 1-4
Select a definition (the numbered buttons may also be clicked)
.TP
.B Esc / q
Quit; in the definition popup, dismiss it
(space and Enter also dismiss it)
.PD
.SH FILES
.TP
.B /lib/temple/vocab.dict
The dictionary, converted from the TempleOS AutoComplete
dictionary data: records of a marker byte
(1 word, 2 definition, 3 pronunciation, 4 part of speech, 5 extra)
each followed by a UTF-8 string and a NUL.
.TP
.B /lib/temple/vocab.ndx
Byte offset into
.B vocab.dict
of each entry that has at least one definition, one decimal number
per line.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/temple/vocabulary.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR temple (1),
.IR tone (2),
.IR wm (1)
.SH BUGS
The original quizzed the live AutoComplete word list; this uses the
same dictionary converted to a static file.
